      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "This war has been going on for nearly five years, and somehow the one thing that never seems to run out is money\n\nZelensky keeps asking for more, Europe keeps sending it, and ordinary Europeans, especially Ukrainians, are the ones paying the price with their lives.\n\nEurope doesn't want this war to end, and Zelensky doesn't seem much interested in ending it either. They just keep pretending they're working toward peace while the money keeps flowing\n\nHundreds of billions have been poured into this war, and we're supposed to believe there aren't massive financial and political incentives to keep the whole thing going? Come on\n\nAnd don't forget the fact that Ukraine didn't even had election since 2019\n\nThe political elites get to make speeches, demand more money, and pretend they're saving the world while ordinary families bury their children\n\nIt's absolutely insane how this has become an endless cycle of asking for money, sending money, and sending people to die, with no end in sight",
      "quote": {
        "author": "elonmusk",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103567689515954176/aR-Kjpp4_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-24 01:04:00",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-23T17:04:00.000Z",
        "id": "2113677835244044748",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Elon Musk",
        "text": "What’s actually going on in Ukraine is that there is a massive incentive difference between the elites and the people. \n\nThe former have grown very rich off the hundreds of billions flowing to Ukraine, while the latter’s children are conscripted to die in trenches.",
